1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,500
Your cat's slow blink might be a reply.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:05,204
In one experiment, owners
slow-blinked at their cats.

3
00:00:05,204 --> 00:00:07,551
Cats half-blinked and
narrowed their eyes more

4
00:00:07,551 --> 00:00:10,000
than when owners sat
nearby without interacting.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,784
In a second experiment, an unfamiliar
researcher slow-blinked at cats.

6
00:00:13,784 --> 00:00:18,000
The cats were then more likely to approach
her hand than after a neutral face.

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,333
A slow blink is not one long stare.

8
00:00:20,333 --> 00:00:23,466
It is a series of
half-blinks, then a prolonged

9
00:00:23,466 --> 00:00:26,000
narrowing or full closure of the eyes.

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,153
The authors suggest this may
be positive communication.

11
00:00:29,153 --> 00:00:32,191
They also caution that more
research is needed before

12
00:00:32,191 --> 00:00:35,000
firm conclusions about
the cat's emotional state.

13
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
So try one slow blink from a
comfortable distance, then watch.

14
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,355
If the cat looks away or
stays tense, give it space.

15
00:00:42,355 --> 00:00:45,000
The blink is an invitation, not a demand.
